<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Project Planning & Scheduling</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Deliver projects on time with integrated scheduling tools that connect your high-level baseline to daily 
            execution in the field.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Master Programme and Critical Path</h2>
        <p>
            Build comprehensive project schedules using integrated Gantt charts with support for complex task 
            dependencies and sub-programmes. The system automatically identifies the Critical Path (CPM), highlighting 
            the activities that directly determine the project's completion date. Maintain multiple baselines 
            to track schedule evolution and analyze the impact of changes over the project's duration.
        </p>
        <p>
            S-curve visualizations provide an immediate view of progress against the original plan, 
            accounting for both work completion percentages and labor expenditure. This dual tracking 
            ensures that the project's "physical" progress aligns with its "financial" progress 
            expectations.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Resource Planning and Look-Aheads</h2>
        <p>
            Bridge the gap between executive programmes and site-level co-ordination with rolling look-ahead 
            schedules. 2-week and 4-week programmes provide the granular detail needed by site 
            engineers and subcontractors to coordinate material deliveries, plant hire, and labor 
            movements with precision.
        </p>
        <p>
            Resource loading features allow for the allocation of specific labor teams and plant 
            assets to schedule activities. This identifies potential resource bottlenecks and 
            under-utilization across the project portfolio, enabling proactive reallocation of 
            key assets where they generate the most value.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Delay Analysis and EOT Support</h2>
        <p>
            When delays occur, document them in real-time with integrated delay event logs. Link 
            delay occurrences directly to schedule activities and site diary entries, providing 
            the evidence required for formal Extension of Time (EOT) applications. This 
            structured approach to delay analysis minimizes the risk of liquidated damages 
            and ensures a clear audit trail for any contractual claims.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

